,{"sectionKey":"load_fatigue_recovery","sourceUrl":"https://www.power-systems.com/pdf/PSystems_DigitalGuide_Jan18.pdf","sourceTitle":"2018 Buyers Guide","sourcePublisher":"Power Systems","sourceKind":"manufacturer_instruction","evidenceQuality":72,"claims":["No-bounce slam balls and rebounding medicine balls have materially different retrieval, catch, and repeat-cadence behavior.","Slam Ball Scoop Slam must track ball mass and rebound type, high-intent slams, catches, side balance, technical speed loss, shoulder and trunk fatigue, floor contacts, recovery between sets, and weekly ballistic-ball volume."]},{"sectionKey":"constraints","sourceUrl":"https://www.acefitness.org/continuing-education/certified/june-2019/7306/medicine-balls-an-ace-integrated-fitness-training-reg-model-workout/","sourceTitle":"Medicine Balls: An ACE Integrated Fitness Training Model Workout","sourcePublisher":"American Council on Exercise","sourceKind":"expert_instruction","evidenceQuality":78,"claims":["Medicine balls, wall balls, dead-weight balls, and slam balls are not interchangeable for every impact task; implement construction and rebound behavior must match the exercise.","Require an intact slam-rated ball, a floor rated for repeated impact, safe overhead and rebound clearance, stable footing or knee padding, athlete separation, and no bystanders in the impact, rebound, or retrieval zone."]},{"sectionKey":"dosage","sourceUrl":"https://www.acefitness.org/resources/pros/expert-articles/6941/five-exercises-to-help-your-clients-develop-power/","sourceTitle":"Five Exercises to Help Your Clients Develop Power","sourcePublisher":"American Council on Exercise","sourceKind":"expert_instruction","evidenceQuality":76,"claims":["High-velocity medicine-ball power work is commonly delivered in low-repetition sets with enough recovery to preserve output.","For power delivery, use roughly three to five sets of three to five high-quality slams or two to five per side with 60–180 seconds between sets; 